{#
   THE STATE CELL — the coloured word that says how a row is doing (S134i).

   ⚠️ **It takes a SIGNAL, never a class name and never a stored word.** That
   distinction is not pedantry here: `/admin/machines` used to write
   `class="status-badge {{ machine.statut }}"`, so a machine whose stored value
   was `idle` got a class no stylesheet defined and printed its English database
   word inside a chip that stayed green. The caller says what the row MEANS; this
   file decides what that looks like.

   Parameters:

     label   the word, already translated ("Disponible", "En panne")
     signal  go | wait | caution | stop | muted
             go      it is available / done / confirmed
             wait    it is in progress / booked / queued
             caution it needs attention soon / is due / is pending
             stop    it is broken / cancelled / banned / overdue
             muted   it is archived, closed, or simply not applicable
     reason  passed to `_cell_empty` when there is no label

   The vocabulary is green/amber/red plus grey, on purpose: the operator pointed
   out it is the traffic-light convention and worldwide, and it became the
   `_state_chip` signal names.

   🔴 **Measured, 2026-08-11:** before S134i every one of these chips rendered
   `rgb(212, 200, 210)` in dark mode — `--color-text-light`, on its own coloured
   tint — because `style.css` repainted every `<span>` inside `.admin-panel` with
   an `!important` that no local rule can outrank. The fix is in that blanket's
   `:not()` list, not here. If a chip ever goes grey again, look there first.
#}
{% if label|default('') %}
    {# ⚠️ `is-go` … `is-muted`, not `.active` / `.disponible` / `.annulee`. The
       old classes ARE the stored words, which is why they were being
       interpolated from database values in the first place, and why the set has
       eleven French and English synonyms sharing four colours. Those stay
       defined for the pages S134j has not reached; nothing new should use them. #}
    {% set _class = {
        'go':      'is-go',
        'wait':    'is-wait',
        'caution': 'is-caution',
        'stop':    'is-stop',
        'muted':   'is-muted',
    } %}
    <span class="status-badge {{ _class[signal|default('muted')]|default('is-muted') }}">{{ label }}</span>
{% else %}
    {% include 'site/_cell_empty.html.twig' with {reason: reason|default('cell.no_state')} only %}
{% endif %}
